WEBVTT

00:22:58.018 --> 00:23:00.750
CM: The number one thing
that an algorithm does,

00:23:00.774 --> 00:23:04.355
is it mechanically aggregates
all the information.

00:23:04.379 --> 00:23:07.184
That's the number one advantage it has

00:23:07.208 --> 00:23:09.498
over what intuitive judgment does.

00:23:09.522 --> 00:23:13.211
Humans are notoriously bad
at doing that in a systematic way,

00:23:13.235 --> 00:23:15.441
and we think we're better
than we actually are.

00:23:15.465 --> 00:23:18.296
AG: Your algorithm beats
the human argument.

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.363
You're comparing the algorithm to humans

00:23:20.387 --> 00:23:22.378
who have not been trained in biases,

00:23:22.402 --> 00:23:25.170
who have not followed
good structured-interview practices,

00:23:25.194 --> 00:23:26.971
who don't have a scoring key.

00:23:26.995 --> 00:23:31.073
And so, isn't it possible
that once we train humans,